# DURABLE REPRO — D10 exclusivity hole A6: the WRITER is the method RECEIVER,
# and the reader is an element view of that same receiver.
#
# `b.grow_from(b.items.get(0).unwrap())` calls an `&self` method — a writer of
# `b` — while passing a live borrow of `b.items[0]` as its argument.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C backend, `--sanitize`): `gg check`
# clean, then AddressSanitizer heap-use-after-free in `gorget_string_copy_cow`
# inside `Bag__grow_from`. `check_call_aliasing` is handed only the ARGS; the
# receiver is walked separately and never enters the participant set, so the
# one place that is definitely being written is invisible to the overlap test.
#
# INTENDED: REJECTED at `gg check` with `E_BorrowConflict`. The receiver's
# implicit sigil is part of the participant model: `&self` is a writer, bare
# `self` a reader.
#
# The 4096-push loop FORCES a real reallocation.
#
#
# ORACLE (ggdef, measured this session): ACCEPTS this program and prints the
# pre-mutation value. ggdef is a definitional INTERPRETER with value semantics,
# so a reallocation cannot invalidate anything and this UAF class is
# structurally unobservable in that lane — it is NOT the authority here. The
# intended REJECT comes from the ratified D10 exclusivity ruling, which ggdef
# owes as part of the same landing (Core #9). Full note in
# `sound_excl_getchain_local.gg`.
# Cited from TODO.md (CoW / ownership / High): the D10 "one exclusive writer"
# structural-chokepoint entry, hole #2.
struct Bag:
    Vector[String] items

equip Bag:
    void grow_from(&self, String seed):
        int i = 0
        while i < 4096:
            self.items.push("filler-padding-to-force-a-real-reallocation")
            i = i + 1
        print(seed)

void main():
    Bag b = Bag(Vector[String]())
    b.items.push("alpha-heap-forced-payload")
    b.grow_from(b.items.get(0).unwrap())
